#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:3
msgid "Testing Guide"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:5
msgid ""
"This page describes how LLVM-libc tests are organized, what a test for a new "
"function should cover, and how to make sure the test you wrote is the test "
"that ran. {ref}`build_and_test` lists the build commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:9
msgid "Kinds of tests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:11
msgid ""
"All tests are declared with `add_libc_test` or one of its wrappers, in the "
"`CMakeLists.txt` next to the test source under `libc/test/`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:0
msgid "Rule"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:0
msgid "Use it for"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:0
msgid "`add_libc_test`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:0
msgid ""
"The default. The same source is built against the system libc in overlay "
"mode and against LLVM-libc's own startup code and headers in a full build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:0
msgid "`add_fp_unittest`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:0
msgid "Floating point tests. Adds the floating point test helpers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:0
msgid "`add_integration_test`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:0
msgid ""
"Behavior that needs a real process from start to finish: program startup, "
"`exec`, thread-local storage, threads still running at exit. Full build only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:20
msgid ""
"A test may be restricted with `OVERLAY_ONLY` or `FULL_BUILD_ONLY`. Use these "
"only when the test cannot work in the other mode. An entrypoint that is full-"
"build only does not need the option: its test is skipped automatically in "
"overlay mode because the entrypoint is missing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:25
msgid ""
"Each test names the `SUITE` it belongs to, and each test directory defines a "
"suite named after it, such as `libc-ctype-tests`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:28
msgid "Running tests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:41
msgid ""
"While developing, run the specific test. Before considering a change "
"finished, run `check-libc`, because a change in one area sometimes affects "
"another."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:44
msgid ""
"A change should pass in both an overlay build and a full build. Keeping one "
"build directory for each mode makes this quick."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:47
msgid "Making sure your test ran"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:49
msgid ""
"CMake silently drops a test when one of its dependencies is not available on "
"the target: an entrypoint that is not in `entrypoints.txt`, a missing "
"startup object, or a missing MPFR library. A dropped test does not fail. It "
"is simply not part of `check-libc`, which then passes. This is expected "
"behavior, since some entrypoints are unavailable on some targets and should "
"not report an error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:55
msgid "To avoid reporting a pass for a test that never ran:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:57
msgid ""
"Configure with `-DLIBC_CMAKE_VERBOSE_LOGGING=ON`. CMake then prints a line "
"starting with `Skipping` for every test dropped because of a missing "
"entrypoint or startup object. Tests dropped because MPFR is missing are "
"reported only at CMake's verbose log level (`--log-level=VERBOSE`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:61
msgid ""
"Run the test by its own target name. If the target does not exist, the test "
"was dropped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:63
msgid ""
"Watch it fail first. Run the test before the implementation is complete, or "
"break the implementation on purpose, and confirm that the test fails."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:66
msgid "What to test"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:68
msgid "Test the behavior that LLVM-libc is responsible for."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:70
msgid ""
"**A function that is a thin wrapper around a system call** needs one test of "
"success and one of failure. That shows the arguments reach the kernel in the "
"right order and that an error is reported through the return value and "
"`errno`. Do not test path resolution, permission checks, or other behavior "
"the kernel implements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:75
msgid ""
"**Logic that lives in the libc** is tested thoroughly, including the "
"boundary cases. A search of `PATH` in `execvp` and the buffering in `stdio` "
"are examples."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:78
msgid ""
"**Tests for C standard functions use only C standard functions** to set up "
"and check their state. A test for `fgets` should not need `pipe` or `fdopen`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:82
msgid ""
"A test file is generally named after the function it tests. When one file "
"tests several functions that only make sense together, name it after all of "
"them, for example `popen_pclose_test.cpp`. This is a general rule and not an "
"absolute one: `fileop_test.cpp` covers many `stdio` functions under one "
"descriptive name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:88
msgid "Conventions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:90
msgid "Test suite names start with `LlvmLibc`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:91
msgid ""
"Call the LLVM-libc functions through the `LIBC_NAMESPACE` namespace to avoid "
"pulling in the system libc's implementations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:93
msgid ""
"Include types and macros through the proxy headers in `libc/hdr/`, as in "
"implementation code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:95
msgid ""
"For functions that set `errno`, derive the fixture from `ErrnoCheckingTest` "
"and check results with the `Succeeds` and `Fails` matchers from `test/"
"UnitTest/ErrnoSetterMatcher.h`. The fixture asserts that `errno` is zero "
"when each test ends, so a test that expects an error must consume it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:99
msgid ""
"Compare with `ASSERT_EQ`, `ASSERT_NE`, and the other typed assertions, not "
"`ASSERT_TRUE(a == b)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:101
msgid ""
"Use `cpp::scope_exit` to close files and remove temporary files when a later "
"assertion could return early."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:104
msgid "Tests must not depend on their environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:106
msgid ""
"Tests run on developers' machines, in containers, under emulators, and on "
"buildbots, as different users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:109
msgid ""
"**Paths.** Create every path with `libc_make_test_file_path`, including "
"paths that are meant not to exist. Never assume that a fixed absolute path "
"such as `/nonexistent` is absent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:112
msgid ""
"**Privileges.** Avoid tests whose result depends on the user's privileges. "
"Where that is unavoidable, the test must pass both as root and as an "
"ordinary user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:115
msgid ""
"**System state.** Do not rely on `/proc` being mounted or on network access."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:116
msgid ""
"**Emulators.** When the tests are run through an emulator, that is, when "
"`CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR` is set, the build defines "
"`LIBC_TEST_UNDER_EMULATOR` for test code (see `libc/cmake/modules/"
"LLVMLibCTestRules.cmake`). Guard a test that cannot work under emulation "
"with `#ifndef LIBC_TEST_UNDER_EMULATOR`, as `libc/test/src/sys/mman/linux/"
"mlock_test.cpp` does, instead of loosening what it expects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:124
msgid "Disabling a test"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:126
msgid ""
"Disable as little as possible, and say why. Which mechanism to use depends "
"on how much of the test file is affected:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:129
msgid ""
"**A whole test cannot pass in some configuration.** Disable it in CMake with "
"a condition that names the configuration. The condition can be as specific "
"as CMake can express, for example one architecture on baremetal with a "
"particular math option enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:133
msgid ""
"**A small part of a larger test file is affected.** Guard that part with "
"`#ifdef` on a macro that states the reason, so the rest of the file keeps "
"running. The `printf` tests are the model: the tests for an optional feature "
"are wrapped in checks such as `LIBC_COPT_PRINTF_DISABLE_FLOAT`, which `libc/"
"test/src/stdio/CMakeLists.txt` passes to the test under the same condition "
"as to the library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:140
msgid ""
"Which one fits is a judgment call. In both cases, link an issue that tracks "
"re-enabling the test when the cause is a bug. Do not comment out a test body "
"or wrap it in `#if 0`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:144
msgid "Death tests and null checks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:146
msgid ""
"`EXPECT_DEATH` and `EXPECT_EXITS` tests, including the tests that check "
"`LIBC_CRASH_ON_NULLPTR`, are wanted. Some CI configurations currently skip "
"them with `LIBC_TEST_SKIP_DEATH_TESTS`; that is a limitation of those "
"configurations to be fixed and not a reason to leave such tests out."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:151
msgid "Other test frameworks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:153
msgid ""
"Tests are written against LLVM-libc's own framework in `libc/test/UnitTest/"
"`, which is a subset of GoogleTest. Some downstream users compile the same "
"tests with GoogleTest or a compatible framework, so stay within that subset "
"and the matchers LLVM-libc provides. Keeping a downstream framework working "
"is the responsibility of that downstream."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:159
msgid "Math tests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:161
msgid ""
"Tests that compare against MPFR (`NEED_MPFR`) run in overlay mode only, "
"because MPFR is not yet supported in a full build. A math change must be "
"tested in an overlay build with MPFR installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:164
msgid ""
"Tests in `libc/test/src/math/smoke/` do not need MPFR. They are the math "
"tests that run in full builds and on baremetal and GPU targets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:166
msgid ""
"Tests in `libc/test/src/math/exhaustive/` take a long time and are not run "
"by `check-libc`. The author of a math change runs them locally. See {ref}"
"`math_function_guidelines`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:170
msgid "Fuzzing and benchmarks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:172
msgid ""
"Neither is required for a new function today. Ideally, security-sensitive "
"functions have fuzz tests and performance-sensitive functions have "
"benchmarks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/testing_guide.md:175
msgid ""
"Fuzz tests live in `libc/fuzzing/` (see {ref}`fuzzing`). A migration of the "
"fuzz tests to [FuzzTest](https://github.com/google/fuzztest) is being "
"considered. The benchmarks under `libc/benchmarks/` are unmaintained, apart "
"from the GPU benchmarks in `libc/benchmarks/gpu/`."
msgstr ""
